  "body": "What changed\n- package-appimage/flatpak/snap/linux.sh and package-macos.sh take the logotype PNGs from `assets/logo/icons/` instead of `assets/ui/cube.png` (the .deb/rpm also install hicolor 16-512 sizes; the .icns uses the matching size per entry, only 1024 px is scaled up from 512).\n- `scripts/installer/camcraft.iss`: `SetupIconFile` is the logotype `.ico`.\n- Windows exe icon: `crates/ui/build.rs` embeds `camcraft.ico` via `winresource` (a `cfg(windows)` build-dependency, default features off). A missing resource compiler only warns.\n- Wasm `/app/` favicon not changed (the site favicon is the docs site's; not in this PR).\n- `PROCESS_VERSION` 61 -> 62 (touches `xtask/` tests).\n\nNEEDS THE MAINTAINER'S YES: new build dependency `winresource` (Cargo.lock +1 crate) and a `build.rs` change; decision in `docs/decisions/1461-logo-packaging.md`.\n\nPinning test: `package_paths_tests::packages_and_installer_carry_the_logotype_icons` (xtask); the existing `package_paths_tests` still pass (4/4).\n\nHow tested\n- `cargo test -p xtask package_paths`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo build -p camcraft-ui --bin camcraft-ui` on Windows (build script ran, winresource compiled); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nNot exercised\n- `cargo xtask gate quick`: the Cargo.lock change makes it fall back to the batch tier (~20 min); not run, only the targeted checks above.\n- The installer (ISCC), macOS `.icns` on a real Mac (sips/iconutil), Linux packages and desktop entries on a real desktop, and that the built exe actually shows the icon in Explorer (not looked at).\n- UI-visible (icon): screenshots owed.\n\nChangelog: The Windows exe, installer, macOS .icns and Linux packages carry the CamCraft logotype icon (#1461, PR #M)\nEffort: medium (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1461\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
